# Client-side routing: the app is one page and holds its own view state, so any
# path that is not a file must return index.html rather than a 404.
#
# /api and /auth are NOT listed. They are handled by Pages Functions, which run
# before this file is consulted; adding them here would be inert at best and,
# if the Functions ever failed to deploy, would quietly answer API calls with
# index.html instead of failing loudly.
/*  /index.html  200
